Conclusion:
  Through m=9, the AP/interval regular tournament is the unique chi=2 class.
  The m=7 non-circulant regular class exists, but chi=3; it is not a
  tight regular alternative with a new chi.  At m=9, all 14 non-AP
  regular classes have chi=3.  Thus chi does add beyond vertex-transitivity
  (AP vs Paley at m=7), and the full small census strengthens the LRC
  reading: regular tightness points to the minimally cyclic chi=2 AP orbit.
